# Everything here is excluded from the build context — the set of files Docker
# uploads to the daemon before it reads the Dockerfile. Two reasons to keep it
# tight: the build starts faster, and nothing unwanted can be COPYed by accident.

# --- Secrets. Never bake an .env into an image; the file survives in every
# --- layer and anyone with the image can read it back out.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.p12
*.jks

# --- Build output. The image compiles the project itself in stage 1, so a local
# --- target/ is not just useless here, it would be stale.
target/

# --- IDE, editor and agent scratch directories
.idea/
.vscode/
.settings/
.qoder/
.vault/
*.iml
.classpath
.project

# --- Files that only ever matter on your machine
mvnw
mvnw.cmd
.mvn/
*.log
docker-compose.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# --- Docs, screenshots and demo assets: no running container needs them
docs/
vibe_images/
README.md
TEST.md
HELP.md
ORACLE_SQL_SETUP.md
AGENTS.md
LICENSE
.gitattributes
.gitignore

# --- Git history (the classic way an accidental secret leaks into an image)
.git/

# NOTE: pom.xml and src/ are deliberately *not* ignored — stage 1 builds from them.
